The soil is made up of:

- **solid components** such as organic matter and stones;
- **water** containing minerals;
- and **air**.

The soil is also home to organisms a few millimetres in size:

- **mites**;
- tiny worms called **nematodes**;
- **insect larvae**.

The soil also shelters small soil animals (**invertebrates**) such as:

- **woodlice** and **earthworms**;
- **termites** and **ants**;
- **centipedes**, **millipedes** and **spiders**.

**Crop residues** provide organic matter. Depending on the quantity, they can be added:

- either to the **compost bin** to make compost;
- or under the mulch of the **pathways** to form a **surface compost**.
